      "name": "Meriken Park",
      "description": "Meriken Park (メリケンパーク, Meriken pāku) is a waterfront park located in the port city of Kobe, Hyōgo Prefecture, Japan.  The park features the Kobe Port Tower, Kobe Maritime Museum, and a memorial to victims of the Great Hanshin earthquake.  The name of the park comes from the word \"American,\" which was commonly translated as \"Meriken\" during the Meiji era.",
